WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.180
Some ideas are too odd to schedule, and too interesting to delete. Give them a little garden.

2
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:14.197
Welcome to Compost Club. The sample uses fictional scraps and unchanged Gemma recordings.

3
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:21.913
Two scraps grow into one possibility. This is recorded mode, with no live generation.

4
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:32.398
Here is a real Gemma result for these exact inputs. You decide whether the combination is worth keeping.

5
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:41.773
Open its roots to read both parents and their exact fragments. The original model text stays attached.

6
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:50.949
Keep what makes you curious. Your collection is saved locally, in this browser.

7
00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:59.849
Reload: your keeper is still here. Export Markdown with its sources and recorded label.

8
00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:08.083
Earn a slot every fifteen minutes, up to three. The demo clock skips time, without generating.

9
00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:17.353
Four B passed all twenty-four format checks. Browser models failed. You still judge usefulness.

10
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:27.451
Explore the public code and evidence. Live generation needs local Ollama. Let your wild ideas ferment.
